tr - translate or delete bytes

SYNOPSIS
    tr set1 set2
    tr -d set

DESCRIPTION
    Copy standard input to standard output. Replace each byte in set1 with
    the byte at the corresponding position in set2. If set2 is shorter,
    repeat its last byte as needed.

    With -d, discard the bytes in set. A set consists of literal bytes and
    ranges such as a-z.

EXAMPLES
    tr a-z A-Z < /README

SEE ALSO
    cut(1), grep(1)
